 "notes": "Observed exclusion from Fig. 7 (e-print file sidecar_limit_plot_2021_final_prl_oct11.pdf), extracted from the vector boundary of the purple 'This work' filled region. Axes calibrated from tick labels; cross-checked against the plotted KSVZ/DFSZ lines (read 7.1e-15 / 2.7e-15 at 19.84 ueV vs expected ~7.8e-15 / 3.0e-15, i.e. <10% scale accuracy). Masses converted from the bottom frequency axis via m=h*f; the figure's top mass axis is internally offset from h*f by ~0.9 MHz, so the frequency axis was used. Resulting span 4796.8-4799.5 MHz matches the abstract. Paper assumes axions are all the local dark matter with rho=0.45 GeV/cc (canonical density, no rescaling). Confidence level not explicitly stated in the paper; 90% assumed as the standard haloscope convention. ADMX sidecar cavity with a JTWPA first-stage amplifier; deepest exclusion ~1.6e-13 GeV^-1 near 19.842 ueV.",
